COPY public.community_proposals (id, "trackingId", title, description, "problemStatement", "suggestedSolution", "categoryId", locality, status, "submitterId", "moderatedById", "moderatedAt", "internalModerationNotes", "publicExplanation", "officialResponse", "officialResponseById", "officialResponseAt", "supportCount", "createdAt", "updatedAt", "isModerated") FROM stdin;
8d5facd3-94b8-4924-a826-e045633c81cd	PROP-2026-00010	Establish Solar-Powered Public Reading Gazebo in Sector 4 Park	Construct a sheltered open-air reading pavilion with solar rooftop panels, energy-efficient LED night illumination, and weather-resistant wooden benches to promote neighborhood community study and outdoor gathering.	The public park in Sector 4 has substantial underutilized lawn space but lacks shaded seating or quiet study spaces for neighborhood students and senior citizens.	Install an eco-friendly modular wooden gazebo with 1.2kW solar panels, integrated USB charging points, and nighttime warm-white lighting.	38d60f7b-1420-49cf-831d-0f639592d853	Sector 4 Community Park, East Lawn	ACCEPTED_FOR_CONSIDERATION	18fc9424-3582-45bb-a779-e55e3dea5926	\N	\N	Site inspection conducted by Town Planning field unit on Oct 14. Concept feasible within municipal park development guidelines.	The proposal aligns with the municipal green amenities plan and has passed initial feasibility checks.	The Town Planning Department acknowledges and accepts this proposal for technical feasibility analysis. It has been referred to the engineering cell for inclusion in the forthcoming ward amenity prioritization study.	f0f9a4f3-263c-4bc4-b975-73d3dfe9fe29	2026-10-15 14:30:00	0	2026-10-18 02:05:08.984	2026-10-18 02:05:08.984	f
11828473-ec0f-443c-9e40-1700d904aa23	PROP-2026-00011	Add Raised Pedestrian Zebra Crossing with High-Visibility Signage near Silver Oak School	Install a 10cm raised tabletop pedestrian crossing with reflective yellow-and-white road paint, flashing solar warning beacons, and school-zone speed limit signage.	Vehicles traveling along 5th Main frequently exceed safe speeds directly in front of the primary school gate during morning drop-off hours.	Install an engineered raised speed table crossing that naturally forces vehicles to slow down to 20 km/h while allowing children to cross at curb level.	63f77d3d-f11a-4219-aff6-200007851ed2	5th Main Road, Opposite Silver Oak School Gate 2	PUBLISHED	327aa575-4bbe-44ad-a91e-d6a5c4351333	\N	\N	Verified not a complaint: suggests new traffic-calming infrastructure rather than reporting a pothole. Approved for public listing.	\N	\N	\N	\N	0	2026-10-18 02:05:09.01	2026-10-18 02:05:09.01	f
b6fc3ce8-a326-4e25-a714-03cb948ce7c4	PROP-2026-00012	Deploy Color-Coded Segregated Waste Bins along Commercial Market Walkway	Install 12 pairs of color-coded wet/dry dual-stream stainless steel dustbins along the high-footfall bazaar corridor.	\N	\N	e2b3175c-4aa8-401c-bec6-fcc27fdc04ae	Station Road Commercial Market Corridor	UNDER_REVIEW	03bb1e30-4a8d-44c3-a430-b151dfa2d2b2	\N	\N	Pending review by Sanitation Department zonal coordinator.	\N	\N	\N	\N	0	2026-10-18 02:05:09.017	2026-10-18 02:05:09.017	f
